※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4710
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4710 LANG_ARRAY_NOT_COPIED

※ What an array joined onto a list puts in it is a copy of its elements, made by copying
※ their bytes -- so it is an array copied, and an array is copied only where its elements
※ are all of their value (4710).  A string points into room something else keeps, and a
※ second holder of that room is a question the lifetime rules answer one value at a time.
※ A list of strings is joined onto as a list, `l ⧺← [s]`, which copies each one deep.

let std := ⎕import("std")

@[startup]
fn main(init: std.Init) → u6:
    let words: str⟦2⟧ = ⟦"one", "two"⟧ in ⎕static
    let l: mut [str] = []
    l ⧺← words
    if #l = 2: 0u6 else: 1u6
